\DOC UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC

\TYPE {UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal whose conclusion equates an explicitly built event-trace term
with an application of a defined event function.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal {A ?- t = u} in which one side is a
concrete list/{APPEND} expression of trace events and the other is a call of a
named event-trace function, it proves the equation outright; the assumptions
{A} are left untouched and play no role.
{
      A ?- t = u
    ================ UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC
      (no goals)
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, this is the only outcome — the tactic closing such an
equational goal — and the goals always carry a large context of assumptions
that is neither added to nor removed from.

\ENDDOC
